<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.13.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01103</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.13.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>47d7fa48-eb66-4663-bd3f-df8748b53b14</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00002">
        <exercise id="_79dcc02b-722b-43fa-b175-5d7a3be32eb9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <newline/>
            <para id="para-00002">The graph of function \(H\) shows the height, in meters, of a rocket \(t\) seconds after it was launched.
          <para id="para-00003"><figure id="fig-00001"><media alt="Function on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_16_13_01.svg"/></media></figure></para>
          <para id="para-00004">Find \(H(0)\) in meters.</para>
         </para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00005">Correct! 15 meters, This is the height that the rocket was launched.</para>
            <para id="para-00006">Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00007">The correct answer is 15 meters. This is the height that the rocket was launched.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_401eedc3-c9dd-4ed4-8ce4-c33756bc18bb" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00008">Which of the following describes the domain of this function?</para>
            <para id="para-00009">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00010">\(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 35\)</para>
            <para id="para-00011">\(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4.5 \)</para>
            <para id="para-00012">\(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 2\)</para>
            <para id="para-00013">\(15 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 35\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00014">Correct! \(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4.5\).; The domain includes all values from 0 to approximately 4.5, \(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4.5\).</para>
            <para id="para-00015">Try again. Revisit activities 4.13.2-4.13.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00016">The correct answer is \(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4.5\).; The domain includes all values from 0 to approximately 4.5, \(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4.5\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_9d5fb4c0-2545-417f-bb2f-b1720b557e40" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00017">Which of the following describes the range of this function?</para>
            <para id="para-00018">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00019">\(0 \leq \mathrm{y} \leq 35\)</para>
            <para id="para-00020">\(0 \leq \mathrm{y} \leq 4.5 \)</para>
            <para id="para-00021">\(0\leq \mathrm{y} \leq 2\)</para>
            <para id="para-00022">\(15 \leq \mathrm{y} \leq 35\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00023">Correct! \(0\leq y\leq35\); The range includes all values from 0 to 35 meters, \(0\leq y\leq35\).</para>
            <para id="para-00024">Try again. Revisit activities 4.13.2-4.13.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00025">The correct answer is \(0\leq y\leq35\). The range includes all values from 0 to 35 meters, \(0\leq y\leq35\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_308650af-809d-41dc-99a1-98177f84e23c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <newline/>
            <para id="para-00026">Which of the following describes the domain of the function graphed below?</para>
            <para id="para-00027">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00028">\(0 \leq x \leq 9 \)</para>
            <para id="para-00029">\(0 \leq x \leq 4\)</para>
            <para id="para-00030">\(2 \leq x \leq 7\)</para>
            <para id="para-00031">\(2 \leq x \leq 4\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00032">Correct! \(2≤x≤7\); The domain is all values from at least 2 to a maximum of 7, \(2≤x≤7\).</para>
            <para id="para-00033">Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00034">The correct answer is \(2≤x≤7\); the domain is all values from at least 2 to a maximum of 7, \(2≤x≤7\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_54e556fe-abbd-4d44-9fe1-5e2eae99e5db" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <newline/>
            <para id="para-00035">Which of the following describes the range of the graph below?</para>
            <para id="para-00036">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00037">\(2 \leq y \leq 4 \)</para>
            <para id="para-00038">\(2 \leq x \leq 4\)</para>
            <para id="para-00039">\(2 \leq y \leq 7\)</para>
            <para id="para-00040">\(2 \leq x \leq 7\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00041">Correct! \(2≤y≤4\); The range is all values from at least 2 to a maximum of 4, \(2≤y≤4\).</para>
            <para id="para-00042">Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00043">The correct answer is 2≤y≤4. The range is all values from at least 2 to a maximum of 4, 2≤y≤4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="fbedf477-1e0e-4f57-85b8-283e720f9c26" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <newline/>
            <para id="para-00044"><emphasis>Select four</emphasis> of the values of the range for the function \(h\), graphed below.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00045">Correct! -3, -2, 2, 4</para>
            <para id="para-00046">Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00047">The correct answers are -3, -2, 2, 4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_825d31c6-a7df-4505-a96d-d1ca287623d0" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <newline/>
            <para id="para-00048">Which of the following is the domain of the function graphed below?</para>
            <para id="para-00049">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00050">\(-5 \leq x \leq 5 \)</para>
            <para id="para-00051">\(-5 \leq x \leq 7\)</para>
            <para id="para-00052">\(-5 \leq y \leq 5\)</para>
            <para id="para-00053">\(-5 \leq y \leq 7\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00054">Correct! \(-5≤x≤5\)</para>
            <para id="para-00055">Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00056">The correct answer is \(-5≤x≤5\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1cc90588-8a4b-4dd4-8ace-97732fc4dbe6" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <newline/>
            <para id="para-00057">Which of the following represents the domain of the function graphed below?</para>
            <para id="para-00058">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00059">\(y \geq 5 \)</para>
            <para id="para-00060">\(x \geq 5 \)</para>
            <para id="para-00061">\(y \geq 2 \)</para>
            <para id="para-00062">\(x \geq 2\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00063">Correct! \(x≥2\)</para>
            <para id="para-00064">Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00065">The correct answer is \(x≥2\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_86d3ccd0-8185-44eb-aa19-e218144f4a7b" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            <newline/>
            <para id="para-00066">Which of the following represents the range of the function graphed below?</para>
            <para id="para-00067">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00068">\(y \geq 5 \)</para>
            <para id="para-00069">\(x \geq 5 \)</para>
            <para id="para-00070">\(y \geq 2 \)</para>
            <para id="para-00071">\(x \geq 2\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00072">Correct! \(y \geq 5 \)</para>
            <para id="para-00073">Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00074">The correct answer is \(y≥5\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
